  animalName: Manatee
  educationalText: Manatees drift through mangrove channels to graze on seagrass
    and munch on mangrove leaves that hang near the water's surface. They also use
    these sheltered, shallow waterways as safe resting spots and warm-water refuges
    during cooler months.
